mbet</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abilmambet was a Kazakh khan of the Middle Juz from about 1739 until his death in 1771, residing at Turkestan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abimael-guzman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abimael-guzman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abimael Guzmán</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abimael Guzmán was a Peruvian philosophy professor who founded and led the Maoist Shining Path, known to his followers as Chairman Gonzalo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abimilki"><span class="enc-name">Abimilki</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abimilki was king of Tyre in the 14th century BCE, during the Amarna period, when the city was a vassal of Egypt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abiodun"><span class="enc-name">Abiodun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abiodun was an Alaafin, or king, of the Oyo Empire who reigned c. 1770–1789.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abipa"><span class="enc-name">Abipa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abipa was an Alaafin of Oyo who, around 1610, led the return of the Oyo court to its old capital Oyo-Ile after a long exile.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abish-khatun"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abish-khatun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abish Khatun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abish Khatun was the last ruler of the Salghurid dynasty of Fars, in southern Iran, placed on the throne as a child in 1263 under Mongol supervision.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abishemu-i"><span class="enc-name">Abishemu I</span><spa