-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The abolition of the Atlantic slave trade refers to the outlawing of the transatlantic trade in enslaved Africans, beginning with the British Slave Trade Act of 1807…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-ottoman-sultanate"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abolition-of-the-ottoman-sultanate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abolition of the Ottoman sultanate</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The abolition of the Ottoman sultanate was the decision of the Grand National Assembly in Ankara in 1922 to end the office of sultan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abomey"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abomey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abomey</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Abomey is a town in southern Benin, the capital of the Kingdom of Dahomey from the seventeenth century until 1894.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abonnema"><span class="enc-name">Abonnema</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Abonnema is a town in Rivers State in the Niger Delta of Nigeria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-australians"><span class="enc-name">Aboriginal Australians</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Aboriginal Australians are the Indigenous peoples of mainland Australia and Tasmania, whose ancestors have lived on the continent for at least 50,000 years.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-tasmanians"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aboriginal-tasmanians.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aboriginal Tasmanians</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Aboriginal Tasmanians are the Indigenous people of Tasmania, isolated from the mainland when rising seas formed Bass Strait about 10,000 years ago.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aboud-jumbe"><span class="enc-name">Aboud Jumbe</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aboud Jumbe was a Zanzibari politician who became president of Zanzibar and first vice-president of Tanzania after the assassination of Abeid Karume in 1972.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abraha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abraha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abraha</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abraha was an Aksumite general who seized power in Himyar, in Yemen, in the 530s and ruled it, nominally as a vassal of Aksum, until about 570.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abraham-accords"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abraham-accords.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abraham Accords</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 2020</span><span class="enc-snip">The Abraham Accords are agreements, brokered by the United States, by which Israel established diplomatic relations with Arab states, beginning with the United Arab…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abraham-crijnssen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abraham-crijnssen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abraham Crijnssen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abraham Crijnssen was a Dutch naval commander from Zeeland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abraham-davel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abraham-davel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height